# JSON.stringify of an object with a proven layout, in a loop, does not call the built-in. A string builder is taken from the pool by two loads and two stores.
# LOOP-LABEL: loop #
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[point]] = Load(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:indexedContiguousProperties, {{*}}:GetArrayElement)
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[pooled]] = Load(b@{{*}}, offset = {{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:collectorState, {{*}}:StringBuilderBegin)
# LOOP-NEXT: Branch(b@[[pooled]], Terminal, {{*}}:StringBuilderBegin)
# LOOP-NEXT: Successors: Then:#{{*}}, Else:Rare:#
# The writer that was compiled for the layout is called directly with the object and the builder, and says whether it could write all of it.
# LOOP: Int32 b@[[written]] = Patchpoint(b@[[point]]:Register({{*}}), b@[[builder]]:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallDirect)
# LOOP: Int32 b@[[isWritten]] = Equal(b@[[written]], $1(b@{{*}}))
# LOOP: Branch(b@[[isWritten]], Terminal)
# One more call makes the string out of the builder.
# LOOP: Int64 b@{{*}} = Patchpoint(b@[[builder]]:Register({{*}}), {{*}}, resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), ExitsSideways{{*}}:StringBuilderFinish)
# LOOP-LABEL: end of loop
# The writer is called at one place. The built-in itself is not called in this loop: an object that the writer gave up on leaves it by a rare edge.
# CALLS-LABEL: loop #
# CALLS-NOT: :CallBuiltin)
# CALLS-COUNT-1: ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallDirect)
# CALLS-NOT: :CallDirect)
# CALLS-NOT: :CallBuiltin)
# CALLS-LABEL: end of loop
# The counts hold calls, whose moves follow the calling convention: not for Windows.
# A turn calls, so the loop polls on every turn: one of the patchpoints.
# X64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 42, patchpoints: 5, rare instructions: 5
# ARM64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 39, patchpoints: 5, rare instructions: 5
